{"cluster_id": "C-4290", "topic": "The bounded-walk follow-up measured approximately 444 logs", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B027-157"], "canonical_claim": "The bounded-walk follow-up measured approximately 444 logs per second as the concurrent writer/walker throughput boundary, motivating a stop-at-round-start-tail design independent of concurrent writes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-15"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4291", "topic": "T15 GC validation results", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B029-007", "B029-008", "B030-068"], "canonical_claim": "On the T15 re-validation binary, GC completed 64 `Success` folding rounds with an average duration of 100.7 seconds, a minimum of 2.8 seconds, and a maximum of 433.5 seconds; the preceding T14 run completed zero rounds in 42 minutes. Additionally, The T15 validation completed 64 successful and four deferred rounds in 118.7 minutes; round duration was bounded between 2.8 and 433.5 seconds, and `CasGcProbeADue` equaled `CasGcProbeAPerformed` at four.; The T15 re-validation measured `CasGcProbeADue = 4`, `CasGcProbeAPerformed = 4`, `CasGcProbeASkipped = 0`, and `CasGcRefScanDisagreements = 0`; the document concludes that the sampling cadence was adequate once folding rounds were bounded.", "issue_ids": ["PROBE-A-CADENCE-UNIT"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-stage-a-RESULTS.md#t15-revalidation", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-29-gc-perf-audit-soak.md#before-after"]}
