{"cluster_id": "C-4293", "topic": "The transient-classifier audit found 217 Formats/ throw", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B029-046"], "canonical_claim": "The transient-classifier audit found 217 `Formats/` throw sites and zero transient sites there; across the CA tree it found approximately 58 transient sites, of which 50 already use upstream-retryable classes, five use `INVALID_STATE`, and three use `ABORTED` in GC.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-29-ca-transient-classifier-audit.md#headline"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4294", "topic": "CasPrecommitReleaseUnproven counts precommits whose release is not", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B029-062"], "canonical_claim": "`CasPrecommitReleaseUnproven` counts precommits whose release is not proven, not confirmed leaks; it is an upper bound on residue because an `Uncertain` removal may later settle and an unresolved promote may have committed without leaving a precommit.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-part-write-release-seam.md#counter-meaning"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4295", "topic": "relink refusal storm", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B029-077", "B030-058", "B030-086"], "canonical_claim": "The old `CasRefLedger::confirmExactRef` path proved relink availability only about 17% of the time under sustained writes, with approximately 92,000 refusals versus 19,531 proven operations; one run recorded 248,400 refusals in about 32 minutes and a peak of 9,219 per minute. Additionally, The T14 run produced 248,400 relink-refusal exceptions cluster-wide in about 32 minutes, with a peak of 9,219 per minute on one node; the refusal storm was essentially the whole `NETWORK_ERROR` population and was unrelated to GC correctness. Additionally, The T14 draft measured about 92,000 refusals versus 19,531 proven confirms, approximately 17% availability, and an independent GC audit measured 248,400 refusals cluster-wide with a peak of 9,219 per minute.", "issue_ids": ["RELINK-CONFIRM-BUSY-LANE"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-29-relink-confirm-per-ref-draft.md#measured-problem", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-29-gc-perf-audit-soak.md#watch-libunwind", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-relink-reoffer-redesign.md#measured-problem"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4296", "topic": "The relink observability contract defines CasRelinkProven, CasRelinkChanged", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B029-102"], "canonical_claim": "The relink observability contract defines `CasRelinkProven`, `CasRelinkChanged`, `CasRelinkUnknown`, `CasRelinkRecoveryBudgetRefused`, and `CasRelinkAnswerRejected`; `CasRelinkAnswerRejected` should be approximately zero in a healthy cluster.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-relink-reoffer-redesign.md#observability"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4297", "topic": "The query profiler samples every 10 ms", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B030-048"], "canonical_claim": "The query profiler samples every 10 ms while the global background profiler samples every 10 s, so raw frame counts across the two sides are not comparable; the weighted 15-minute sample was about 332 s of query-side CPU versus 11,790 s of background CPU.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-29-gc-perf-audit-soak.md#cautions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4298", "topic": "The T14 GC leader on ch1 completed", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B030-050"], "canonical_claim": "The T14 GC leader on ch1 completed zero rounds in 41 minutes 32 seconds and was still inside the same round when it was killed; ch2 recorded 248 lease rounds with `acquired=0` and `steal_allowed=248`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-29-gc-perf-audit-soak.md#headline"]}

